  "status": "Four candidate44 failing fixtures are corrected and pass focused qualification. The full NATS matrix and five other candidate44 failing tests remain unresolved; no package completion is claimed.",
  "root_causes": [
    "The two batch-header tests publish before their publisher account route receives the stream subscription; the creation reply arrives through a separate API route. The existing event-based route barrier establishes the required ordering.",
    "LastSequenceBySubject ignores every asynchronous publication acknowledgement. PublishAsyncComplete closes on errors too, so the subsequent sequence assertions can observe an uninitialized stream.",
    "ConsumerNumPending creates its consumer before asynchronous stream persistence completes; its snapshot can legitimately contain zero messages. A control using the real stream atomic-publication lock reproduces this on both storage engines and proves correct state after acknowledgements."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Join the existing route-interest barrier before the two batch header tests and the last-sequence fixture.",
    "Retain and verify every setup PubAck, including the stream and sequence, before sequence assertions or consumer creation.",
    "Add two regression controls for consumer creation ordering and failed-publication completion."
